try>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA MASATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOYODA HARUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMAMATSU PHOTONICS K. K.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, MASATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYODA, HARUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA MASATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOYODA HARUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, MASATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYODA, HARUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A high-speed vision sensor comprises an analog-to-digital converter array (13) including analog-to-digital converters (210) corresponding to respective lines of photodetectors (120) of a photodetector array (11), and a parallel processing system (14) consisting of processing elements (400) and shift registers (410) corresponding to the respective photodetectors (120).  Since processing elements (400) carry out the image processing between adjacent pixels by parallel processing at high speed, independently of the operation in the shift registers (410), the processing and shifting can be performed efficiently.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un capteur de vision ultra-rapide, qui comprend un ensemble numériseur (13), constitué de numériseurs (210) correspondant aux différentes rangées de photodétecteurs (120) d'un ensemble photodétecteur (11), et un système de traitement parallèle (14), constitué d'éléments de traitement (400) et de registres à décalage (410) correspondant aux différents photodétecteurs (120). Comme les éléments de traitement (400) traitent les images entre pixels adjacents par un traitement parallèle ultra-rapide, indépendant du traitement dans les registres à décalage (410), le traitement et le décalage s'effectuent de manière efficace.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>